\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Is the following relatively consistent with ZFC?

Every C*-algebra $A$ that has a unique irreducible representation up to the
unitary equivalence is isomorphic to the algebra of compact operators on some
Hilbert space.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{http://aimpl.org/settheorycstar/6/}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Is the following relatively consistent with ZFC?

Every C*-algebra $A$ that has a unique irreducible representation up to the
unitary equivalence is isomorphic to the algebra of compact operators on some
Hilbert space.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 20001476 (AIM-FUNCTIONAL\_ANALYSIS-0035). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{http://aimpl.org/settheorycstar/6/}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:20001476}

